  "statement": "Overnight, offload labels a thread only when it plainly holds several subjects a person would want to see apart: it groups rows that share one, names the group the way the rows do, uses a label the thread already has, and leaves a thread about one thing, and a row that belongs to no group, alone.",
  "why": "025. A sort nobody asked for is only welcome when it is obviously right; a thread wrongly split is a correction, and Activity's Undo is a remedy rather than a licence.",
